==Icelandic==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|is|áttu||less formal|}}

===Etymology===
From second person of ''[[eiga#Icelandic|[að] eiga]]'' "[[own|[to] own]]" (= ''[[átt#Icelandic|[þú] átt]]'' "[you] own") + ''[[þú#Icelandic|þú]]'' "[[you]]". Literally meaning "you own...?" or "do you own...?".

===Phrase===
{{head|is|phrase|head=[[átt]] [[þú]]...?}} (+[[accusative]])

# [[do you have]]...?, [[have you got]]...?
#: {{ux|is|[[afsakið|Afsakið]], [[en#Icelandi|en]] '''átt þú''' [[mjólk]]?|[[excuse me|Excuse me]], [[but]] '''have you got''' [[milk]]?}}

